---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { launch } from '../data/launch';

// One source for the visible Q&A and the FAQPage JSON-LD, so they never drift apart.
// Answers are HTML (one string per paragraph); the JSON-LD gets the same text without tags.
const mail = '<a class="nz-link" href="mailto:noozealarm@gmail.com">noozealarm@gmail.com</a>';

const topics = [
    {
        id: 'alarm',
        title: 'The alarm',
        items: [
            {
                id: 'what-is-nooze',
                q: 'What is Nooze?',
                a: [
                    'Nooze is a no-snooze alarm clock and sleep tracker for Android. To turn an alarm off, you complete a short wake-up challenge. It also estimates how you slept using your phone’s sensors or a compatible wearable, can ring at an estimated lighter moment inside a wake window you choose, and rewards on-time mornings with XP, streaks and wake duels with friends.',
                ],
            },
            {
                id: 'no-snooze',
                q: 'Why is there no snooze button?',
                a: [
                    'By design. The alarm only stops when you finish one of nine wake-up challenges: math, memory, shake, steps, reading a sentence aloud (on supported phones), scanning a QR code or barcode, tapping an NFC tag, typing or a photo task. You set the difficulty for each alarm: easy, medium or hard.',
                    'QR, photo and NFC challenges offer a math problem after 2 minutes, so you’re never stuck. A few minutes after you dismiss the alarm, a wake-up check asks if you’re still up. Ignore it and the alarm rings again.',
                ],
            },
            {
                id: 'smart-wake',
                q: 'How does smart wake work?',
                a: [
                    'Pick a wake window of 15, 20 or 30 minutes for an alarm. Nooze looks for an estimated lighter moment of sleep inside that window and rings then, using your phone’s motion sensor, the optional microphone or a connected wearable. These are estimates, not measurements. If it can’t pick out a clear one but did notice some movement or sound, it rings in the last few minutes of the window. If it notices nothing at all, the alarm rings at the time you set.',
                    'Sunrise Wake can also warm your screen from dark into a soft sunrise glow, so you are not met by a bright flash.',
                ],
            },
            {
                id: 'xp-and-friends',
                q: 'How do XP, streaks and friends work?',
                a: [
                    'Getting up on time earns XP. Streaks, achievements, journal entries and your morning routine checklist add more, and leaderboards for XP, streaks and achievements show how you compare.',
                    'Add friends to start wake duels: whoever gets up on time more often wins. You can also pick a wake-up buddy, who gets one nudge if you miss your wake-up check, or join a squad of up to four that shares a streak.',
                ],
            },
            {
                id: 'smart-home',
                q: 'Does Nooze work with smart home devices?',
                a: [
                    'Yes, with Premium. Nooze connects to Home Assistant, Tuya, Tellur or any webhook. Choose an event, such as an alarm ringing or being dismissed, sleep tracking starting, or Nooze estimating that you’ve fallen asleep, and the action it should trigger, like switching on the lights. The message carries the event and the time, never sleep or health data.',
                ],
            },
        ],
    },
    {
        id: 'sleep',
        title: 'Sleep tracking',
        items: [
            {
                id: 'sleep-tracking',
                q: 'How does sleep tracking work?',
                a: [
                    'Leave your phone near the bed overnight. Nooze uses its motion sensor and, if you allow it, the microphone, or sleep and heart-rate data from a compatible band or watch through Health Connect.',
                    'In the morning you see your sleep duration, estimated sleep phases, an approximate sleep quality score and any snoring or noise events, with weekly trends and bedtime consistency over time. A shared-bed mode helps when you sleep next to someone, and a wearable-only mode relies on your watch’s data alone.',
                ],
            },
            {
                id: 'wearables',
                q: 'Does Nooze work with my watch or fitness band?',
                a: [
                    'If your band, watch or its app writes sleep or heart-rate data to Android Health Connect, Nooze can read it. It reads only those two data types, never writes anything back, and keeps the data on your phone. Health Connect is optional; without it, Nooze uses your phone’s sensors.',
                    'There’s also a Wear OS companion with a next-alarm tile, and your alarm can ring on the watch.',
                ],
            },
            {
                id: 'medical',
                q: 'Is Nooze a medical device?',
                a: [
                    'No. Nooze is a wellness app. Sleep phases, the sleep quality score, snoring and noise events and heart-rate values are estimates for general wellness, not medical advice. If you’re worried about your sleep or health, talk to a doctor.',
                ],
            },
        ],
    },
    {
        id: 'account',
        title: 'Account and privacy',
        items: [
            {
                id: 'sync',
                q: 'What syncs if I sign in on another phone?',
                a: [
                    'Your profile and progress, not your sleep data. Sign in with Google or email and your profile, XP, streaks, achievements, friends, duels and squads come with you. Alarms, sleep sessions, recordings, Health Connect data and journal text stay on the phone they were made on.',
                    'You don’t need an account at all: Nooze works as a guest.',
                ],
            },
            {
                id: 'privacy',
                q: 'Is my data private and secure?',
                a: [
                    'Sensor, microphone, calendar and Health Connect data stay on your phone, along with your alarms and journal text, in an encrypted database. If you create an account, your profile, XP and social activity are stored so they work across phones and with friends.',
                    'There are no ads and no data sales. Usage analytics never receive sleep, health or audio data. The <a class="nz-link" href="privacy.html">privacy policy</a> lists everything.',
                ],
            },
            {
                id: 'delete-account',
                q: 'How do I delete my account?',
                a: [
                    'In the app, open the Profile tab, scroll to the bottom and tap Delete Account. Your account and cloud data are deleted straight away. Without the app, email ' + mail + ' from your account’s address with the subject “Delete my Nooze account” and it’s done within 30 days.',
                    'Deleting your account doesn’t cancel a Google Play subscription, so cancel that in Google Play. The <a class="nz-link" href="account-deletion.html">account deletion page</a> has the details.',
                ],
            },
        ],
    },
    {
        id: 'pricing',
        title: 'Pricing and platforms',
        items: [
            {
                id: 'free',
                q: 'Is Nooze free?',
                a: [
                    'Yes, with no ads. The free version includes unlimited alarms with smart wake, all nine wake-up challenges, the wake-up check, sleep tracking with weekly trends, XP, streaks, friends, wake duels and 6 themes.',
                    'Premium is optional: €1.99 a month or €13.99 a year, about 41% less than paying monthly. It adds 6 more themes with animated backgrounds, advanced sleep analytics, the full sleep sound library, smart home integrations and a spoken morning briefing with the weather, your next alarm and your first event of the day. Cancel any time in Google Play.',
                ],
            },
            {
                id: 'platforms',
                q: 'Which platforms does Nooze support?',
                a: [
                    `Android. Nooze Sleep Tracker &amp; Alarm is out now on <a class="nz-link" href="${launch.playUrl}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Play</a>, with a Wear OS companion for your watch. An iPhone version is in the works.`,
                ],
            },
        ],
    },
];

const total = topics.reduce((n, t) => n + t.items.length, 0);
const pad = (n) => String(n).padStart(2, '0');
const plain = (html) => html.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '').replace(/&amp;/g, '&');

const faqLd = {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: topics.flatMap((t) =>
        t.items.map((it) => ({
            '@type': 'Question',
            name: it.q,
            acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: it.a.map(plain).join(' ') },
        })),
    ),
};
const crumbLd = {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://noozealarm.com/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'FAQ', item: 'https://noozealarm.com/faq.html' },
    ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
    title={"FAQ: smart alarm and sleep tracker questions | Nooze Alarm"}
    description={"Answers to common questions about Nooze: wake-up challenges, smart wake, sleep tracking, wearables, privacy, account deletion and Premium pricing."}
    keywords={"nooze faq, smart alarm questions, sleep tracker help, alarm app faq, nooze pricing, nooze privacy, sleep tracker and alarm questions"}
    canonical={"faq.html"}
    ogTitle={"Nooze FAQ: questions about the no-snooze alarm"}
    ogDescription={"Answers to common questions about Nooze, the no-snooze alarm and sleep tracker for Android."}
    active={"faq"}
>

  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqLd)} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(crumbLd)} />
  </Fragment>

<main id="main" class="flex-1">
    <PageHeader
        compact
        title="Frequently asked questions"
        lede="How the no-snooze alarm works, where your sleep data lives and what Premium adds."
    />

    <section class="faq nz-section--tight">
        <div class="nz-container faq-grid">
            <aside class="faq-aside">
                <nav class="faq-index" aria-label="FAQ topics" data-spy>
                    <p class="nz-meta faq-index-label">{total} questions, 4 topics</p>
                    <ol>
                        {topics.map((t) => (
                            <li>
                                <a href={`#${t.id}`}>
                                    <span class="faq-index-name">{t.title}</span>
                                    <span class="faq-index-count">{pad(t.items.length)}</span>
                                </a>
                            </li>
                        ))}
                    </ol>
                </nav>
            </aside>

            <div class="faq-body">
                {topics.map((t) => (
                    <section class="faq-group" id={t.id} aria-labelledby={`${t.id}-title`}>
                        <h2 class="faq-group-title" id={`${t.id}-title`}>{t.title}</h2>
                        <div class="faq-list">
                            {t.items.map((it, i) => (
                                <details class="qa" id={it.id} open={t.id === 'alarm' && i === 0}>
                                    <summary>
                                        <span class="qa-q">{it.q}</span>
                                        <span class="qa-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                    </summary>
                                    <div class="qa-a">
                                        {it.a.map((p) => <p set:html={p} />)}
                                    </div>
                                </details>
                            ))}
                        </div>
                    </section>
                ))}

                <div class="faq-ask">
                    <p class="faq-ask-q">Didn’t find your answer?</p>
                    <p class="faq-ask-body">
                        Email <a class="nz-link" href="mailto:noozealarm@gmail.com">noozealarm@gmail.com</a>. The developer usually replies within 24–48 hours.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
    // Deep links: open the targeted question (and keep it open on hash changes).
    function openFromHash() {
        const id = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1));
        if (!id) return;
        const el = document.getElementById(id);
        if (el instanceof HTMLDetailsElement) el.open = true;
    }
    openFromHash();
    window.addEventListener('hashchange', openFromHash);

    // Topic index: mark the topic currently under the reading line.
    const nav = document.querySelector('[data-spy]');
    if (nav && 'IntersectionObserver' in window) {
        const links = new Map();
        nav.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('a[href^="#"]').forEach((a) => {
            const target = document.getElementById(a.hash.slice(1));
            if (target) links.set(target, a);
        });
        const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
            entries.forEach((e) => {
                if (!e.isIntersecting) return;
                links.forEach((a) => a.removeAttribute('aria-current'));
                links.get(e.target)?.setAttribute('aria-current', 'true');
            });
        }, { rootMargin: '-30% 0px -65% 0px' });
        links.forEach((_, target) => io.observe(target));
    }
</script>

<style>

    .faq { padding-top: clamp(56px, 7vw, 104px); }
    .faq-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 8fr);
        gap: clamp(40px, 6vw, 96px);
        align-items: start;
    }
    .faq-aside { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 40px); }

    /* Topic index */
    .faq-index-label { margin: 0 0 18px; }
    .faq-index ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .faq-index li { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .faq-index a {
        position: relative;
        display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px;
        min-height: 52px; padding: 15px 0;
        color: var(--fg-2); font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500;
        transition: color 0.25s var(--ease-out), padding-left 0.45s var(--ease-out);
    }
    .faq-index a::before {
        content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 50%;
        width: 14px; height: 2px; margin-top: -1px; border-radius: 1px;
        background: var(--red);
        transform: scaleX(0); transform-origin: left;
        transition: transform 0.45s var(--ease-out);
    }
    .faq-index a:hover { color: var(--fg); }
    .faq-index a[aria-current] { color: var(--fg); padding-left: 26px; }
    .faq-index a[aria-current]::before { transform: scaleX(1); }
    .faq-index-count { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-3); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

    /* Questions */
    .faq-group { scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 24px); }
    .faq-group + .faq-group { margin-top: clamp(64px, 7vw, 104px); }
    .faq-group-title {
        margin: 0 0 22px;
        font-size: clamp(26px, 2.4vw, 34px); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.1;
    }
    .faq-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--line-2); }

    .qa { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 24px); }
    .qa summary {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 32px; align-items: center; gap: 24px;
        min-height: 44px; padding: 24px 0;
        list-style: none; cursor: pointer;
        -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
    }
    .qa summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
    .qa summary::marker { content: ''; }
    .qa-q {
        font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(19px, 1.55vw, 22px); font-weight: 500;
        letter-spacing: -0.015em; line-height: 1.3; color: var(--fg);
    }
    .qa-icon {
        position: relative; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 999px;
        color: var(--fg-2); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line-2);
        transition: transform 0.55s var(--ease-spring), color 0.3s var(--ease-out), box-shadow 0.3s var(--ease-out);
    }
    .qa-icon::before, .qa-icon::after {
        content: ''; position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%;
        width: 12px; height: 1.5px; margin: -0.75px 0 0 -6px; border-radius: 1px;
        background: currentColor;
    }
    .qa-icon::after { transform: rotate(90deg); }
    .qa summary:hover .qa-icon { color: var(--fg); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line-3); }
    .qa[open] .qa-icon { transform: rotate(45deg); color: var(--red); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--red-line); }

    .qa-a { padding: 0 56px 30px 0; max-width: 64ch; color: var(--fg-2); }
    .qa-a :global(p) { margin: 0; }
    .qa-a :global(p + p) { margin-top: 0.9em; }

    /* Smooth open where the browser can animate to height: auto (Chromium 131+). */
    @supports selector(::details-content) {
        @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
            .qa { interpolate-size: allow-keywords; }
            .qa::details-content {
                block-size: 0; overflow-y: clip;
                transition: block-size 0.5s var(--ease-out), content-visibility 0.5s allow-discrete;
            }
            .qa[open]::details-content { block-size: auto; }
        }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
        .qa[open] .qa-a { animation: qa-in 0.5s var(--ease-out) both; }
    }
    @keyframes qa-in { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-6px); } }

    /* Closing prompt */
    .faq-ask {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr); gap: 8px 32px; align-items: baseline;
        margin-top: clamp(64px, 7vw, 104px); padding-top: 28px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    }
    .faq-ask-q { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(22px, 1.9vw, 26px); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--fg); }
    .faq-ask-body { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-2); }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
        .faq-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 56px; }
        .faq-aside { position: static; }
        .faq-index ol { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); column-gap: 20px; }
        .faq-index a[aria-current] { padding-left: 0; }
        .faq-index a[aria-current]::before { transform: scaleX(0); }
        .faq-ask { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    }
    @media (max-width: 520px) {
        .qa summary { gap: 16px; padding: 20px 0; }
        .qa-a { padding-right: 0; }
        .faq-index a { font-size: 15px; }
    }
</style>
